--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DrivetrainHealthPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable DrivetrainHealthDataSource seam whose
methods keep the web hook names at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET
/vehicles, useDrivetrainHealth ← GET /drivetrain/health, useDrives ← GET /drives, useDrivingStats ←
GET /drives/stats, useMotorLatest ← GET /motor/latest, useMotorHistory ← GET /motor, useVehicleLive
← the live SSE isolation-resistance slice). Every derivation (sensors, chartData filter/sort/cap-30,
tempTrend, peak/avg/min-regen power, motorChartData, recommendations, severity colors) is ported
verbatim into the deterministic, unit-tested DrivetrainHealthEngine.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect + the
date RangePicker) and ALL TWELVE web sub-component sections — even though the manifest's automatic
extractor found 0 named panels (the web page delegates to components/drivetrain-health/*), the
honesty covenant's "no scope narrowing" mandate was honored by opening the web source and
reproducing every region in the same data + grouping + order:

  HealthOverview (elevated/critical AlertBanner + the health-summary GlassPanel with state icon,
  headline, motor state, status badge + animated health score), HealthGaugeGrid (the health-score
  RadialGauge + the Motor-Details KVList + a real-time indicator + the Drive-Statistics KVList),
  TemperatureGauges (four severity-tinted value/max gauges), TemperatureMetricCards (four neon
  sensor tiles + health + peak-power), ThermalLoadPanel (four severity MetricBars + four inline
  metrics), LiveMotorStatus (four headline tiles + nine inline RPM/torque/temp/HV-isolation metrics,
  with its own no-telemetry empty), StatorTempChart (3-series line + 60/80 °C refs), TorqueHistory
  (area + 0 ref), TemperatureTrend (line + 35/0 °C refs), PowerOutput (2-series area + 0 ref),
  HealthRecommendations (priority-ordered tips), and DetailCards (Temperature-Details + Power-Summary
  KVLists).

All measurements stay SI canonical in the model (°C / meters / m·s⁻¹ / watts / watt-hours);
conversion to the user's unit preference happens ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared
KMP Units facade + DrivetrainHealthPageFormat (ADR-005). Power stays kW (the web power chart/cards are
never unit-converted — mirrored faithfully). The four charts use the P3 native Swift Charts wrappers
(TSLineChart / TSAreaChart / TSChartContainer), never a WKWebView, and each renders a
ContentUnavailableView empty state instead of the web's hide-on-too-few-points (never a blank region,
ADR-011). Adaptive across macOS/iPad regular width vs. iPhone compact (ADR-002/006): the gauge grid,
metric grid, live tiles, thermal inline grid, and detail cards reflow. Every visible literal resolves
from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (zero hardcoded text; +108 drivetrain.* + route key
+ 3 shared keys surfaced by the page). a11y: accessibilityElement/Label/Value on panels, gauges, and
charts; Dynamic Type via the shared theme; light/dark/increased-contrast via the generated tokens.

Navigation: a new .drivetrainHealth AppRoute case (pathSegment "drivetrain-health") was added so the
page is a real sidebar/tab destination AND deep-linkable at /drivetrain-health without breaking the
sibling DriveScore, which already owns the single .driving route (registering DrivetrainHealth on
.driving would have evicted DriveScore — "no predecessor bypass"). DrivetrainHealthRouteRegistration
registers the host; TeslaSyncApp threads it through the shared registry.

The data sources are request/response + a polled live slice (not a durable SSE replay), so no >2 min
staleness banner applies; the live panel surfaces its own empty state when no snapshot exists.

